  "notes": "Breathy electropop/dance-pop whose one hard researched fact is tessitura: he is \"documented as a baritone instrument, written low with a light head voice used for hooks — an unusually low tessitura for the lane\", so the melody register runs 48—69 with a raised `octaveJumpProb` ceiling for the head-voice hook, which is the lowest topline band in this section and the parameter that keeps this model apart from its neighbours. The drums follow \"programmed kick/clap with a soft-edged transient, 8th-note closed hats, and layered electropop percussion; fills are filtered noise rather than drum rolls\", so the snare transient is soft, `hihat.base` is 8th, `rolls.freqPerBar` is 0 and the fills lane is `riser` percussion instead of a snare ladder. The low end is a synth sub with \"no 808 glide vocabulary\", so no `bass808` block exists and the bassline pumps 8ths on the root at a high `followRootsProb`. Harmony is \"4-bar loops of minor triads with 7th/9th extension\" over a \"pads, plucks and filtered arpeggios\" palette, which is the extension spread and the `arp` counter. \"Toplines are close-mic'd, narrow-range and rhythmically laid back, with the hook often a wordless vocal or a whispered phrase\" is the small `motifPitchCount`, the low density and `endVariation`; \"harmonies are close and dry\" is the low counter density. The arrangement encodes the documented instrumental post-chorus hook and the pre-chorus filter sweep as a drop-out. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says why: \"vocal type, genre turns and palette documented; rhythmic and harmonic detail inferred\". Every drum probability, the humanize pair, the key/scale weighting and `bpm.mode` 112 (the midpoint of the first-named 100—125 band) are INFERRED.",
